added I027, I028, I029, I030, I031, I032, I033; dropped I026. The tip is E021 (Muon + 4@24/4@32 px, 8 epochs: 0.7578, 6.331 s), with 0.48 pp of margin. The top exploit is a compiled, shape-batched Muon step. Eager Muon adds ~1.9 ms/step, mostly launch-bound, and compiling it should save ~0.4 s at no accuracy cost. Next: shift the split to 5@24/3@32 (H2.7, -0.36 s), then explore 16 px first epochs (H2.8.1). Muon momentum 0.85 and tanh-GELU are rebased from older recipes onto the tip, and stale I025/I026 are dropped. For risk control, an extra-seed check (seeds 3-10) on the tip calibrates how much margin later cuts can spend. An NVML observation tests whether the 24 px phase is power-capped (H2.4.1).
